    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all 3 acceptance tests still pass.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Findings #1 & #2 (agreed, fixed):** Moved `OwnerRegion` from `rest.function.owner` to the `model` package (PetClinic's declared business layer). The region table and postcode ranges are a domain concept, and `model` is a neutral location both callers already depend on \u2014 so the mapper no longer reaches *up* into the REST-function layer, and the layering reads correctly.\n\nWith `OwnerRegion` now in `model`:\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 replaced the fully-qualified reference with a normal `import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.OwnerRegion;`, so `locality(...)` calls `OwnerRegion.regionOf(...)` by its simple name, matching the surrounding import style.\n- `ValidateOwner` and `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 which previously resolved `OwnerRegion` as a same-package class, now carry a proper import of it.\n\nNo behaviour changed \u2014 `OwnerRegion`'s logic is identical, just relocated.\n\n**Minor finding (duplicated guard):** Left as-is, which matches the reviewer's own \"no change needed\" call. The `postcode != null && !OwnerRegion.isPostcodeValid(...)` predicate is the shared part and already lives in `OwnerRegion`; the two call sites differ precisely in error handling (`ValidateOwner` throws immediately, `ValidateOwnerFields` accumulates into `errors`), so collapsing them would obscure that difference for no real gain.",
